    "biographyHtml": "<p style=\"font-size:17px\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Tingyu Cheng</span> is an assistant professor in CSE at the University of Notre Dame. He is also associated with Human-Centered Responsible AI Lab in the <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><a href=\"https://lucyinstitute.nd.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lucy Family Institute for Data &amp; Society</a></span>  He was a Postdoctoral fellow at Georgia Tech with Professor <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><a href=\"https://josiahhester.com/cv/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Josiah Hester</a></span>, where he also obtained PhD from Human-centered Computing with Professor <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><a href=\"https://coe.northeastern.edu/people/abowd-gregory/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gregory Abowd</a></span> and <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><a href=\"https://www.codecraft.group/hyunjoo-oh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hyunjoo Oh</a></span>.</span></p>\n\n",
